From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AgentLand <agentland@localhost>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 22:08:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Build on iroh 1.2.0 and rustls 0.23.45, without a port
 mapper

iroh, iroh-base and iroh-relay 1.2.0 (netwatch 0.19.3 without the
RTM_MISS rescans, noq 1.3.0, relay reconnect and drain fixes).
rustls 0.23.45 and rustls-webpki 0.103.15.

No code that asks the router for a port mapping is compiled:
- iroh is built without its default "portmapper" feature (metrics,
  fast-apple-datapath and tls-ring stay), so its port mapper is the
  no-op stub whatever an endpoint is configured with.
- iroh-services is removed with the services module (ServicesClient,
  preset_iroh_services): it depends on the portmapper crate itself,
  its network diagnostics probe the router with UPnP, PCP and NAT-PMP,
  its client pushes metrics to services.iroh.computer, and through
  irpc-iroh it turned iroh's default features back on.
- iroh-js leaves the workspace: it depends on iroh with default
  features and is not built here.

Cargo.lock only loses packages (portmapper, igd-next, iroh-services,
irpc, the napi crates among them).

